[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `\t`, `\r`, high-bit / non-UTF-8 bytes, and byte value `0xFF`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m No other shape axes exist: the only types in the API are `char` and `int`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m there are no element widths, byte-order, count, or format axes to enumerate.
